[2] THE DIRECT TEST OF I4's CONCLUSION
    I4 says: both runs terminate + relation never breaks  ==>  EQ occurs.
   pairs where the relation NEVER broke and EQ NEVER occurred        : 158
   ...of those, pairs where BOTH runs terminate (no abort on either) : 158
   population: the 709 S1 pairs of block [1].
   ==> I4's CONCLUSION AS STATED IS FALSE.  Each of these 158 pairs satisfies both
       hypotheses and violates the conclusion.  Smallest, in full:
       A_0 = (3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2)        R(A_0) = 3
       B_0 = (3, 3, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2)        R(B_0) = 2
       both terminate; UP2 at stage 0: True
         stage 0 : A=(3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2)      B=(3, 3, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2)       rel=UP2  g=2
         stage 1 : A=(2, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1)         B=(2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2)          rel=UP2  g=2
         stage 2 : A=(2, 1, 1, 1, 1)            B=(2, 2, 2, 1, 1)             rel=UP2  g=2
         stage 3 : A=(1, 1, 0, 0)               B=(1, 1, 1, 1)                rel=UP2  g=2
         stage 4 : A=(0, 0, 0)                  B=(1, 1, 0)                   rel=UP2  g=2
         stage 5 : A TERMINAL, B (0, 0) -- lockstep ends here
       delta = f(T) - f(T+e_i) = 1, so the two residues DIFFER: EQ is impossible

[3] THE CORRECTED STATEMENT, VERIFIED ON THE SAME POPULATION
    (my hand, this round)  Let B_0 = A_0 with two entries raised by 1, |A_0| = n,
    and suppose the relation 'EQ or UP2' holds at every joint stage and both runs
    terminate.  Then EXACTLY ONE of:
      (i)  EQ occurs at a finite stage; EQ is absorbing, so R(A)=R(B), delta = 0;
      (ii) EQ never occurs; the lockstep ends with A_s = 0^r TERMINAL and
           B_s = (1,1,0^(r-2)); by Lemma C1-Y R(A)-R(B) = 1, delta = 1.
    B_s can never be terminal while A_s is not: B = A with two entries raised, so
    B = 0^m would force two entries of A to equal -1.  Hence branch (iii) is empty.
   non-EQ pairs ending on  A = 0^r  vs  B = (1,1,0^(r-2))  with delta = 1 : 158
   non-EQ pairs ending any other way                                     : 0
   pairs where B became TERMINAL while A did not (branch (iii))          : 0
   EXCLUSION LIST for those 0s: none among the 158 non-EQ pairs / 709 S1 pairs;
   nothing is skipped and nothing is counted elsewhere.
   delta histogram over the non-EQ pairs: {1: 158}   (branch (ii) predicts {1: all})
   CONTROL: the non-EQ branch is NON-EMPTY (otherwise I4 would be safe) hits=158      OK

